==Bulgarian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|cu|bg}} {{m|cu|чрънъ}}, from {{etyl|sla-pro|bg}} {{m|sla-pro|*čьrnъ}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|bg}} {{m|ine-pro|*krsnos}}. Cognates include Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|црн}}, {{m|sh|crn}}, Slovene {{m|sl|črn}}, Slovak {{m|sk|čierny}}; Norwegian and Swedish {{m|sv|harr||grayling}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|कृष्ण|tr=kṛṣṇá}}, Old Prussian {{m|prg|kirsnan||black}}.

